   "source": [
    "## Download function\n",
    "`download('FORMUE16', PERCENTIL='*', ...)` asks Statistics Denmark for table FORMUE16. Each keyword is one **variable code** and its value selects the rows you want; `'*'` selects all values. This is the same information as the `variables` list in the Lecture 10 API notebook, written more compactly, and it needs no extra package. The result is a DataFrame with one column per variable and the number in `value`.\n",
    "\n",
    "To find the codes of another table, open its table information in your browser, for example [FORMUE15](https://api.statbank.dk/v1/tableinfo/FORMUE15?lang=en&format=JSON)."
   ]
  },
