   "source": [
    "# a. download both tables again, so this cell gives the same result every time it is run\n",
    "percentiles = download('FORMUE16', PERCENTIL='*', **settings)\n",
    "counts = download('FORMUE15', FORMUE='*', DEFINITION='D20', **settings)\n",
    "\n",
    "# b. inspect the first rows of each table\n",
    "print('FORMUE16 (percentiles):')\n",
    "display(percentiles.head())\n",
    "print('FORMUE15 (counts):')\n",
    "display(counts.head())\n",
    "\n",
    "print('Age codes in FORMUE16:', percentiles['ALDER'].unique().tolist())\n",
    "print('Age codes in FORMUE15:', counts['ALDER'].unique().tolist())\n",
    "\n",
    "# c. set the all-adult rows aside for Part 2\n",
    "all_adults = '1802'   # 18 years and over\n",
    "\n",
    "percentiles_all = percentiles.loc[percentiles['ALDER'] == all_adults].copy()\n",
    "counts_all = counts.loc[counts['ALDER'] == all_adults].copy()\n",
    "\n",
    "# d. keep the age groups for the age profiles\n",
    "percentiles = percentiles.loc[percentiles['ALDER'] != all_adults].copy()\n",
    "counts = counts.loc[counts['ALDER'] != all_adults].copy()\n",
    "\n",
    "print('Age groups kept:', percentiles['ALDER'].unique().tolist())\n",
    "print('All-adult rows set aside:', len(percentiles_all), 'percentiles and', len(counts_all), 'brackets')\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "8f95e0f1",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**Interpretation.** \n",
    "\n",
    "FORMUE16 gives one row for each percentile (P1–P99) and age group, while FORMUE15 shows the number of people in each wealth group and age group. FORMUE15 also requires the wealth definition (DEFINITION='D20'), which refers to the 2020 definition. The age code 1802 ("18 years and over") covers all adults. We use these observations for Part 2 and keep the other age groups for the age profiles."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "6ea411c8",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1.2   Plot the Age Profiles\n",
    "Tasks and hints: PDF Section 1.2."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 4,
   "id": "2346d887",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "image/png": "",
      "text/plain": [
       "<Figure size 800x400 with 1 Axes>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# a. percentile codes to numbers ('P10' -> 10)\n",
    "percentiles['p'] = percentiles['PERCENTIL'].str.replace('P', '').astype(int)\n",
    "\n",
    "# b. one row per age group, one column per percentile\n",
    "table = percentiles.pivot_table(index='ALDER', columns='p', values='value')\n",
    "\n",
    "# c. readable age labels in the same order as the rows\n",
    "age_labels = {'1829': '18-29', '3039': '30-39', '4049': '40-49', '5059': '50-59',\n",
    "              '6069': '60-69', '7079': '70-79', '8089': '80-89', '9099': '90+'}\n",
    "table.index = table.index.map(age_labels)\n",
    "\n",
    "# d. plot P10, P50 and P90 by age group\n",
    "fig = plt.figure(figsize=(8, 4))\n",
    "ax = fig.add_subplot(1, 1, 1)\n",
    "for p in [10, 50, 90]:\n",
    "    ax.plot(table.index, table[p]/1e6, marker='o', label=f'P{p}')\n",
    "ax.axhline(0.0, color='black', linewidth=0.8)\n",
    "ax.set_xlabel('Age group')\n",
    "ax.set_ylabel('Net wealth, million DKK')\n",
    "ax.set_title('Net wealth percentiles by age, Denmark 2024')\n",
    "ax.legend();"
   ]
  },
